WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:19.430
Oxford bookworms, starters, the 15th character by Rosemary Bauder, read by Nick Mercer, published and copyright, Oxford University Press 2000.

00:19.480 --> 00:29.510
Chapter 1 Jobs for Today

00:29.560 --> 00:40.390
Every day, lots of different people come to Happy Hills, because there are lots of exciting things to do.

00:40.440 --> 00:45.470
Sally Brown works at Happy Hills in her holiday.

00:45.520 --> 00:50.390
She is a student, and she wants to be a teacher.

00:50.440 --> 01:00.030
I need the money, she tells her family, and it's an interesting job.

01:00.080 --> 01:06.790
But she is always very tired in the evening.

01:06.840 --> 01:12.590
The workers at Happy Hills arrive early in the morning.

01:12.640 --> 01:18.870
They all wear clean green trousers and yellow shirts.

01:18.920 --> 01:26.150
They must smile a lot and be nice to all the visitors.

01:26.200 --> 01:35.710
Every morning, Mr. Parry puts a list of jobs for today in the workers' canteen.

01:35.760 --> 01:40.310
Mr. Parry wears different clothes.

01:40.360 --> 01:57.750
His shirt is green, and his trousers are white, and he wears a red coat with I'm Ken Parry. Can I help you? On his pocket.

01:57.800 --> 02:06.910
The visitors call him Ken, but all the workers call him Mr. Parry.

02:06.960 --> 02:14.750
Today, Sally arrives at Happy Hills at eight o'clock.

02:14.800 --> 02:26.790
On her shirt, there is a picture of a smiling face, and have a happy day in black and red writing.

02:26.840 --> 02:34.950
She goes to the canteen and looks for Mr. Parry's list.

02:35.000 --> 02:38.430
What job am I doing today?

02:38.480 --> 02:47.550
Sally thinks, am I making tea or helping in the children's playhouse?

02:47.600 --> 02:50.830
But Sally is wrong.

02:50.880 --> 03:01.350
The list says, Sally Brown, Connie Cat, Brake, eleven o'clock.

03:01.400 --> 03:10.150
Oh no, thinks Sally.

03:10.200 --> 03:19.710
Nobody likes wearing the costumes, but at Happy Hills, the characters are very important.

03:19.760 --> 03:46.630
The visitors like to take photos of their children with cowboy Joe, Charlie Clown, Baby Blue Eyes, Photo Fill, Big John, Connie Cat, Big Apple, Miss Flower, Edward Elephant, and all their friends.

03:46.680 --> 03:55.990
Sally always asks the same questions, are you very hot in your costume?

03:56.040 --> 04:01.670
And how do you eat and drink?

04:01.720 --> 04:05.270
Edward Elephant has the best job.

04:05.320 --> 04:09.830
He has a bag of water under his costume.

04:09.880 --> 04:14.270
He can spray the visitors with water.

04:14.320 --> 04:21.710
And Photo Fill and Charlie Clown make everybody laugh.

04:21.760 --> 04:25.910
But Connie Cat cannot do that.

04:25.960 --> 04:34.830
She can only say, meow. To the children all day.

04:34.880 --> 04:38.470
Sally looks for her costume.

04:38.520 --> 04:44.710
A tall man in a cowboy costume is standing beside her.

04:44.760 --> 04:48.910
Hello, Sally. Says the cowboy.

04:48.960 --> 04:53.590
It's me, William.

04:53.640 --> 04:56.470
William is a student too.

04:56.520 --> 04:59.870
He is Sally's friend.

04:59.920 --> 05:04.230
Which costume are you looking for?

05:04.280 --> 05:06.630
Connie Cat.

05:06.680 --> 05:09.430
When's your break?

05:09.480 --> 05:11.950
11 o'clock.

05:12.000 --> 05:17.990
Me too.

05:18.040 --> 05:27.990
Chapter Two. Here comes Zapp.

05:28.040 --> 05:30.150
It is 9 o'clock.

05:30.200 --> 05:32.230
The doors open.

05:32.280 --> 05:36.150
But there are not many visitors today.

05:36.200 --> 05:38.990
They all have invitations.

05:39.040 --> 05:42.710
And they show them to Mr. Parry.

05:42.760 --> 05:47.110
A very famous man is coming to Happy Hills.

05:47.160 --> 05:51.110
So Mr. Parry is very excited.

05:51.160 --> 06:01.270
Zapp's coming today. He's opening the new Zappocopter. Says William to Sally.

06:01.320 --> 06:08.910
Stop talking and do some work. Says Mr. Parry.

06:08.960 --> 06:11.550
Zapp is a singer.

06:11.600 --> 06:14.950
Sally loves listening to his songs.

06:15.000 --> 06:18.710
And she has all his CDs.

06:18.760 --> 06:24.110
There is a picture of him in her room too.

06:24.160 --> 06:28.870
The Zappocopter is very exciting.

06:28.920 --> 06:36.310
Zappoc can sit in little helicopters and go up and down very fast.

06:36.360 --> 06:42.590
The visitors stand behind a blue rope and wait for Zapp.

06:42.640 --> 06:50.470
Please stay behind the rope. Says Mr. Parry.

06:50.520 --> 06:54.990
Suddenly there is a noise in the sky.

06:55.040 --> 06:57.310
Everybody looks up.

06:57.360 --> 07:03.430
Zapp's helicopter says William.

07:03.480 --> 07:09.150
The helicopter comes down and Zapp gets out.

07:09.200 --> 07:12.190
He smiles at the visitors.

07:12.240 --> 07:19.590
Oh, he's wonderful. Says a young girl.

07:19.640 --> 07:23.070
She gives Zapp a flower.

07:23.120 --> 07:30.510
He gives her a big smile and says, thank you.

07:30.560 --> 07:35.150
Sally is hot and thirsty in her costume.

07:35.200 --> 07:44.830
She wants to talk too, but Mr. Parry is watching.

07:44.880 --> 07:54.990
Number three, Zapp's new song.

07:55.040 --> 07:59.350
Mr. Parry takes the singer to the Zappocopter.

07:59.400 --> 08:03.910
Zapp cuts the rope.

08:03.960 --> 08:05.670
Thank you, Zapp.

08:05.720 --> 08:12.200
Now please, can you sing for us? Says Mr. Parry.

08:12.280 --> 08:21.070
OK, but the people must help me. He says, he begins to sing.

08:21.120 --> 08:26.790
Everybody knows the song and sings it with him.

08:26.840 --> 08:30.350
Thank you, says Zapp.

08:30.400 --> 08:33.710
You're all wonderful singers.

08:33.760 --> 08:37.310
Now look at this.

08:37.360 --> 08:40.750
He takes a CD out of his pocket.

08:40.800 --> 08:44.630
This is my new song.

08:44.680 --> 08:52.030
He says, please sing it for us. Say the TV, men.

08:52.080 --> 08:54.910
But Zapp smiles.

08:54.960 --> 08:57.230
No, no.

08:57.280 --> 09:03.110
You must come to my big concert next Saturday.

09:03.160 --> 09:08.000
He puts the CD in his pocket again.

09:08.080 --> 09:14.910
Now let's go on the Zappocopter, says Zapp.

09:14.960 --> 09:19.390
He sees a teacher with some children.

09:19.440 --> 09:24.470
Would they like to come too? He asks her.

09:24.520 --> 09:28.790
Of course, says the teacher.

09:28.840 --> 09:33.550
They help the children into the helicopters.

09:33.600 --> 09:37.510
Zapp smiles and smiles.

09:37.560 --> 09:42.430
The photographers take lots of pictures.

09:42.480 --> 09:46.070
Photo fill arrives too.

09:46.120 --> 09:50.190
He is one of the Happy Hills characters.

09:50.240 --> 09:56.190
He takes a photo of the children and sprays them with water.

09:56.240 --> 09:59.910
Everybody laughs.

09:59.960 --> 10:04.080
Zapp is having a wonderful day.

10:04.160 --> 10:07.630
He speaks to the TV people.

10:07.680 --> 10:13.350
The photographers take photos of him with all the characters.

10:13.400 --> 10:16.670
Zapp meets Charlie Clown.

10:16.720 --> 10:19.270
Charlie gives him a flower.

10:19.320 --> 10:23.030
And the flower sprays him with water.

10:23.080 --> 10:26.750
Everybody laughs.

10:26.800 --> 10:29.630
Sally meets Zapp too.

10:29.680 --> 10:32.630
And she is very excited.

10:32.680 --> 10:38.310
But she cannot talk to him because she is wearing her cat costume.

10:38.360 --> 10:41.160
And Mr. Parry is watching.

10:46.040 --> 10:50.680
Chapter four. Where's Zapp's CD?

10:56.840 --> 10:57.790
Come on.

10:57.840 --> 11:01.830
It's 11 o'clock, says William.

11:01.880 --> 11:04.910
Let's go to the canteen for our break.

11:04.960 --> 11:08.790
We've got 10 minutes.

11:08.840 --> 11:14.190
They sit down in the canteen and take off their heads.

11:14.240 --> 11:16.590
Sally is thirsty.

11:16.640 --> 11:20.270
Her face is hot and red.

11:20.320 --> 11:24.430
William is hot and thirsty too.

11:24.480 --> 11:28.830
They have a long drink of cold water.

11:28.880 --> 11:33.750
That's good, William says.

11:33.800 --> 11:37.230
Then he looks at his watch.

11:37.280 --> 11:41.350
10 past 11, he says.

11:41.400 --> 11:43.760
Come on, Sally. Back to work.

11:46.680 --> 11:52.270
They finish their drinks and put their heads on again.

11:52.320 --> 11:57.350
Suddenly, a lot of people come into the canteen.

11:57.400 --> 12:01.750
Watch the matter, says William.

12:01.800 --> 12:06.630
Zapp's CD, says Mr. Parry.

12:06.680 --> 12:10.270
He can't find it.

12:10.320 --> 12:13.470
Everybody is unhappy.

12:13.520 --> 12:17.790
But Zapp is angry too.

12:17.840 --> 12:26.390
That's CD's important, Parry. He says, you must find it.

12:26.440 --> 12:31.670
I'm doing my best, Zapp. Says Mr. Parry.

12:31.720 --> 12:33.990
Don't hit me, please.

12:34.040 --> 12:35.680
I'm doing my best.

12:38.960 --> 12:43.070
A lot of things happen very quickly.

12:43.120 --> 12:46.350
The visitors want to go home.

12:46.400 --> 12:51.790
But suddenly, Mr. Parry closes all the doors.

12:51.840 --> 12:55.990
Nobody can leave. He says.

12:56.040 --> 13:05.350
I'm sorry, but Zapp's CD is very important, and we must find it.

13:05.400 --> 13:09.790
Mr. Parry makes a telephone call.

13:09.840 --> 13:16.230
Very soon, four police arrive in a big white police car.

13:16.280 --> 13:17.680
They ask a lot of questions.

13:20.680 --> 13:24.670
The police look everywhere for the CD.

13:24.720 --> 13:28.830
They read Mr. Parry's list of visitors.

13:28.880 --> 13:36.710
They count the visitors carefully and look in all their pockets and bags.

13:36.760 --> 13:39.470
There is a lot of noise.

13:39.520 --> 13:43.110
People are angry and tired.

13:43.160 --> 13:46.390
They want to go home now.

13:46.440 --> 13:54.310
And Zapp is speaking very quietly into a little black telephone.

13:54.360 --> 14:00.950
Photo fill goes to him and says, smile, please.

14:01.000 --> 14:07.590
Go away, says Zapp angrily.

14:07.640 --> 14:11.790
Now the police want to talk to the workers.

14:11.840 --> 14:19.670
One stays with the visitors, and three police speak to the workers in the canteen.

14:19.720 --> 14:23.310
Zapp comes with the police.

14:23.360 --> 14:29.150
You must find that CD, says Zapp.

14:29.200 --> 14:32.920
We're doing our best, Zapp. Say the police.

14:38.360 --> 14:42.640
Chapter 5, the 15th character.

14:48.800 --> 14:51.840
Sally waits quietly with the other workers.

14:53.920 --> 15:01.950
She looks at Mr. Parry's jobs for today list and counts the names.

15:02.000 --> 15:06.510
There are 29 names on the list today.

15:06.560 --> 15:10.350
15 people are helpers.

15:10.400 --> 15:17.520
They wear green trousers and yellow shirts and help the visitors.

15:17.600 --> 15:26.030
14 people are characters and wear costumes.

15:26.080 --> 15:28.350
Wait a minute.

15:28.400 --> 15:30.470
Think Sally.

15:30.520 --> 15:39.030
There are 14 characters on the list, but there are 15 characters here.

15:39.080 --> 15:45.310
She reads the list again very, very carefully.

15:45.360 --> 15:47.550
Edward Elephant.

15:47.600 --> 15:50.430
Yes, he's here.

15:50.480 --> 15:52.630
Connie Cat.

15:52.680 --> 15:54.630
That's me.

15:54.680 --> 15:57.270
Cowboy Joe.

15:57.320 --> 15:59.230
That's William.

15:59.280 --> 16:01.670
Photo fill.

16:01.720 --> 16:04.190
Yes, he's here.

16:04.240 --> 16:06.230
Big Apple.

16:06.280 --> 16:08.310
Yes.

16:08.360 --> 16:14.470
So laugh a lot and lady love a little.

16:14.520 --> 16:16.550
Wait a minute.

16:16.600 --> 16:24.870
Charlie Clown isn't on the list, but Charlie's here in this room.

16:24.920 --> 16:29.630
Excuse me, Mr. Parry, says Sally.

16:29.680 --> 16:37.150
There are 14 characters on your list, but there are 15 in the room now.

16:37.200 --> 16:43.150
Charlie Clown isn't on the list, but he's here.

16:43.200 --> 16:48.270
Mr. Parry reads the list and counts the characters.

16:48.320 --> 16:54.870
You're right, Sally, he says.

16:54.920 --> 17:01.390
Take off your heads, Mr. Parry says to the characters.

17:01.440 --> 17:04.910
They take off their heads.

17:04.960 --> 17:09.630
Charlie Clown is a woman.

17:09.680 --> 17:16.430
Why are you wearing that costume? Asks Mr. Parry.

17:16.480 --> 17:23.470
The woman begins to run away, but William stops her.

17:23.520 --> 17:30.150
The police take off her costume and find a big pocket.

17:30.200 --> 17:34.030
In it they find Sap's CD.

17:34.080 --> 17:39.270
The singer smiles again.

17:39.320 --> 17:41.870
It is Saturday night.

17:41.920 --> 17:49.150
Sally and William are in London because they're going to Zap's concert.

17:49.200 --> 17:57.110
There are lots of excited people and TV photographers outside the hall.

17:57.160 --> 18:00.600
Everybody wants to hear Zap's new song.

18:01.600 --> 18:08.550
Where are your tickets? Says the man at the door to Sally.

18:08.600 --> 18:13.550
We haven't got any tickets, says Sally.

18:13.600 --> 18:18.550
The man begins to look angry.

18:18.600 --> 18:24.550
Sally smiles and takes something out of her pocket.

18:24.600 --> 18:27.550
Is this invitation okay?

18:27.600 --> 18:31.600
It's from Zap.
